# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST.
#
# This working directory holds personal trading data alongside the source:
# a portfolio, an options journal, capital and risk limits, a scan database,
# and megabytes of cached market data. On a public repository a denylist is
# one forgotten pattern away from publishing a holdings file permanently, so
# everything is excluded by default and the source is added back explicitly.
#
# Adding a new data file requires no change here. Adding a new source file
# that is not a top-level .py DOES — which is the safe direction to fail.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Exclude everything, including directories (git will not descend into an
# excluded directory, so venv/, cache/, finra_cache/ and their contents are
# unreachable and cannot be re-included by the rules below).
*

# ── Re-include the source ──
!*.py
!.gitignore
!README.md

# ── Never, under any circumstance ──
# Redundant against the `*` above; kept explicit so the intent survives any
# future edit that loosens the allowlist.
portfolio.xlsx
options_journal.csv
trading_config.json
rush_algos.db
learned_params.json
squeeze_log*.csv
scenario_log*.csv
stock_log.csv
squeeze_snapshots*.json
catalyst_cache*.json
grading_status.json
grading_runs.log
scoring_config.json
borrow_snapshots.json
borrow_data/
squeeze_*_*.csv
scratch_*.txt
